Enterprise UX/UI Modernization (Production Ready)

http://localhost:3001/dashboard/scanner?tab=agents

You are a Senior Staff Software Architect, Principal Product Designer, Enterprise UX Designer, and Cybersecurity Platform Engineer specializing in enterprise cybersecurity products such as CrowdStrike Falcon, Microsoft Defender XDR, Wiz, Prisma Cloud, Cortex XSIAM, Microsoft Azure Arc, SentinelOne, and Google Security Command Center.

Your task is to redesign the QGuard Helix Agent Collector Scanner into a modern Enterprise SaaS experience that is significantly easier for first-time users while maintaining all existing enterprise capabilities.

Primary Goal

The current Agent Collector Scanner is technically complete but exposes too much information simultaneously.

This creates unnecessary cognitive overload.

The redesigned experience must:

Reduce complexity
Improve onboarding
Reduce learning time
Increase usability
Preserve all enterprise functionality
Follow modern enterprise UX principles
Follow progressive disclosure
Be production-ready

The goal is for a security engineer to install a collector within five minutes without reading documentation.

Core Design Philosophy

The interface must answer only four questions.

How do I create a Collector?
How do I install it?
How do I verify it is connected?
How do I start my first scan?

Everything else must be hidden until needed.

The UI should never overwhelm first-time users.

Advanced users should still have access to every enterprise capability.

